DEVLOG — updates.txt fourth pass (6fe4a65)

THE OVERFLOW BUG, because it will recur: grid-cols-[65%_1fr] overflowed
because a bare '1fr' is minmax(AUTO,1fr) — the column will not shrink below
its content's min-content width. Fixed with minmax(0,1fr) PLUS min-w-0 on
both grid children PLUS max-w-full on the image. Any one of those missing
reintroduces the floor by a different route. Test at 390-1600px and assert
document.scrollWidth == clientWidth.

SIDE RAYS have two perf regimes and the difference is large:
  - behind content (default): blurred rotating blades are effectively free,
    because the backdrop under them is static and gets cached.
  - overlay mode (over live canvases): each blade costs real frames.
    mix-blend-mode:screen measured 19fps and was removed; blade count is
    capped at 4 in overlay mode because 9 cost another ~30fps.
Overlay mode exists only because the hero's right half is an opaque photo,
so rays behind it are invisible.

SPARKLES: gravity defaults to 0 on purpose. ANY shared downward constant
makes the field fall in unison and read as rain. Two things had to change
together — the per-frame integration AND the recycling, because respawning
particles at the top reintroduced the same bias even with gravity at zero.

GOOEY BUBBLES cannot be drawn over browser chrome. Asked and answered: no
z-index, portal or stacking context does it. The burst arc is biased
downward instead so they stay in the page.

